# Call-site ledger of pgvector at 5275164edb3a2847d4a5aec1af5ae90f7dc47b53.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in pgvector.md.
#
# Scope (pgvector.md): requires-python >= 3.10; no runtime dependency. numpy
# and scipy are installed in the trace environment (real names); asyncpg,
# Django, peewee, pg8000, psycopg, psycopg2 and SQLAlchemy are not: their calls
# are named as missing modules by access path (micro-benchmark rules), and a
# missing library calls nothing back. Arguments annotated with a missing
# module's class are named through that annotation.
default reject pgvector.bit.Bit.__eq__, pgvector.halfvec.HalfVector.__eq__, pgvector.sparsevec.SparseVector.__eq__, pgvector.vector.Vector.__eq__: no operand of these comparisons, `in` tests, subscripts or dict and set keys is a package vector; they compare or index ints, floats, strs, bytes, arrays, dicts, lists, typing forms in annotations, numpy dtypes and arrays, or client values that the package converts to floats (the package never puts a vector into a list, dict or set)
default reject pgvector.bit.Bit.__repr__, pgvector.halfvec.HalfVector.__repr__, pgvector.sparsevec.SparseVector.__repr__, pgvector.vector.Vector.__repr__: no formatted, converted or %-formatted value at these sites is a package vector; they are ints, floats, strs, lists and dicts of floats and ints, bytes elements, and exceptions

